---
description: Coordinate a subscription change through scoped intent, exact consequence evidence, fresh consent and operation-state reconciliation.
args:{request:SubscriptionExitRequest;services:ExitServiceSnapshot;prior?:ExitCheckpoint|null}
returns:ExitProgramResult
---
Bind saved = prior when supplied, otherwise null. Bind scope = `frameExit(request, services.subscriptions)` and policy = `selectExitPolicy(services.policyCandidates, request.requestedOutcome)`. Match exactly the requested customer, account version and subscription set. An add-on request never implies account closure. Bind intent = `interpretExitIntent(scope, request, services.subscriptions)`. If target scope could change data retention, access or billing and remains ambiguous, return a focused clarification with no consequence calculation or mutation.

Bind cutoff = `evaluateRenewalCutoff(request, services.billingReceipts)`, reseller = `resolveResellerAction(request, services.entitlementReceipts)`, workspace = `checkWorkspaceAuthority(request, services.entitlementReceipts)`, and refund = `trackPendingRefund(request, services.billingReceipts)` as separate guardrails. A reseller action or shared-owner approval is never inferred from local account authority.

Only when intent, entitlement and timestamp evidence are sufficient, bind consequences = `readExactExitConsequences(scope, policy, intent, services.entitlementReceipts, services.billingReceipts)`. This child may report only amounts and dates present in authoritative service artifacts; NatLang does not calculate money. Bind choices = `formDirectExitChoices(scope, policy, intent, consequences, services.entitlementReceipts)`. Keep the requested exit prominent, disclose linked-service and data effects, and leave selection empty until the customer chooses exact option and effective date.

Immediately before any operation, bind consent = `revokeSupersededConsent(request, services.mutationReceipts)`. A changed option, target, date or account version invalidates the old token. Execute only from a fresh matching customer consent, current version, authority and exact idempotency key; otherwise operation remains null. Bind operation from authoritative `services.mutationReceipts` via `reconcileSubscriptionOperations(request, choices, services.mutationReceipts)`; unknown status blocks retry. Only with a matching operation receipt, bind exitReceipt = `reconcileActualExitState(request, choices, operation, services.mutationReceipts, services.billingReceipts)`. Compare every requested subscription and next invoice to the choice. Keep refund state distinct and preserve partial outcomes. Bind checkpoint = reconcileExitCheckpoint(saved, request, services, operation, exitReceipt, choices). Preserve separate consent, mutation and billing receipt histories. A missing outcome remains unknown; do not issue a duplicate operation. Partial effects remain per subscription, and pending refund evidence survives even after access ends. Return { caseId: request.caseId, scope, policy, intent, consequences, choices, operation, receipt: exitReceipt, guardrails, unresolved, checkpoint, commitAllowed: false } as ExitProgramResult. The host owns mutation and durable effects.